# SHELVED 2026-08-30, out of the build. Delete `note draft` to bring it back.
#
# Superseded by `code/exception.tree`, the same way `code/error.tree` was: every
# exception is a form that is `like exception` and pins its `note`, and a raise
# constructs the form at the `halt`. This module predates that design. It raises
# a plain record through `halt kink`, which the checker now types as passing a
# callee's exception on, not as a raise, so the rust backend hands the record to
# the carrier and refuses. The failures it enumerates map onto the standard
# forms: connection-refused is `refusal`, dns-not-found is `absence`, timeout is
# `timeout`, connection-reset is `outage`. Nothing imports this module.

note draft


form network-kink
  link code, like text
  link note, like text
  link hint, like text, need false

host kink-code
  term connection-refused
  term dns-not-found
  term timeout
  term connection-reset
  term address-in-use
  term tls-error
  term websocket-error
  term body-too-large

task make
  take code, like text
  take note, like text
  take hint, like text, need false
  send back
    make network-kink
      bind code, read code
      bind note, read note
      bind hint, read hint

task throw
  take code, like text
  take note, like text
  take hint, like text, need false
  halt kink
    call make
      bind code, read code
      bind note, read note
      bind hint, read hint
